  "behavior": [
    "Runtime reconstruction restores original provider observations and uses canonical field authority.",
    "Provider field provenance, durable generation links, and excluded-model review candidates retain their own receipts.",
    "Legacy provider layers retain separate record receipts. Active binding selection precedes reconstruction.",
    "Generated change timestamps derive from retained source publication and observation times. Unchanged evidence keeps its payload and generation identity.",
    "Each reconstruction evaluates pricing validity at the current time. Rejection evidence names a stable interval boundary.",
    "Concurrent rebuilds serialize durable publication and activation. Canceled rebuilds cannot publish unfinished candidates.",
    "Provider-only authored definitions do not establish canonical identity. Integration fixtures supply reviewed definitions through a separate catalog source.",
    "Primary selection applies before provider reconciliation, preserving unselected provider evidence. Reconstruction avoids an unused baseline copy."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "CLI and HTTP adapters still need a runtime transaction for manual source observations and shared binding settings.",
    "That transaction must preserve previews, source filters, fresh-mode semantics, strict acquisition, workspace projection, and retained layers.",
    "Complete field presence, scoped deletion, upstream manifest lineage, Starport adoption, and released-pair acceptance remain open.",
    "All 50 primary cases remain UNVERIFIED. CSP3 remains in progress.",
    "The full repository publication gate and required second-model review remain open. No branch push or native CI dispatch occurred.",
    "The consumer capture precedes the final primary-filter and unused-copy corrections. Those corrections add no imports.",
    "CPU profiles cover control-plane test execution. They do not establish gateway latency or a statistically supported performance improvement."
  ],
